WEBVTT

00:00:04.020 --> 00:00:06.560
Hello? Oh, Mr. Sasaki.

00:00:06.560 --> 00:00:07.400
Yes.

00:00:07.690 --> 00:00:10.860
Uh-huh. Did you buy souvenirs for your family?

00:00:11.400 --> 00:00:14.820
<i>I'm Takato Saijo, an extremely popular actor.</i>

00:00:16.070 --> 00:00:18.330
Nitto Talent Agency
Takato Saijo

00:00:16.070 --> 00:00:20.700
No. I'm taking it easy in my own way. Yes.

00:00:20.910 --> 00:00:24.920
<i>Because of my competence, I quickly finished
shooting my commercial here in Hawaii,</i>

00:00:24.920 --> 00:00:28.710
<i>so I decided to spend
the remaining two days just to relax.</i>

00:00:29.250 --> 00:00:31.760
You take it easy too, Mr. Sasaki.

00:00:31.960 --> 00:00:33.550
Right. See you later.

00:00:33.840 --> 00:00:38.510
hug8 "H-Hands off my swim trunks."

00:00:34.720 --> 00:00:38.100
The sound of the waves is so pleasant.
Really soothing.

00:00:38.100 --> 00:00:39.050
<i>Or it should be.</i>

00:00:39.310 --> 00:00:40.470
Takato!

00:00:39.720 --> 00:00:42.180
Mitsuya Production
Junta Azumaya

00:00:40.810 --> 00:00:42.930
I bought some tropical juice!

00:00:43.270 --> 00:00:48.730
<i>But even here, I'm in the grasp
of this terrifying stalker angel.</i>

00:02:22.660 --> 00:02:25.410
What are you doing here?

00:02:25.410 --> 00:02:27.660
This is Hawaii! Not Japan!

00:02:27.660 --> 00:02:30.170
How can I get any rest here, you stalker!

00:02:30.290 --> 00:02:32.330
R-Really, it's just a coincidence.

00:02:32.330 --> 00:02:35.130
I just happened to have
a magazine photo shoot here.

00:02:36.340 --> 00:02:40.010
Always a coincidence with you.
You must buy them by the bunch!

00:02:42.050 --> 00:02:45.390
It's kind of refreshing to make a scene
without anyone knowing who we are, huh?

00:02:45.390 --> 00:02:48.180
It's a popular sightseeing spot,
but we're still in another country.

00:02:48.680 --> 00:02:51.150
That just means we're only on a national level.

00:02:51.350 --> 00:02:52.100
I'm loving this.

00:02:53.980 --> 00:02:58.940
I mean, I love getting to have a date with you
by the light of day and at the beach.

00:02:59.450 --> 00:03:00.570
This is no date, you dummy!

00:03:04.580 --> 00:03:06.240
Tomo, this is so cute!

00:03:06.240 --> 00:03:07.830
Let's buy matching ones!

00:03:08.540 --> 00:03:10.160
Matching stuff is lame!

00:03:08.540 --> 00:03:10.620
Newlywed Couple
Tomo

00:03:08.540 --> 00:03:10.620
Newlywed Couple
Miki

00:03:10.160 --> 00:03:12.880
To commemorate our honeymoon!

00:03:12.880 --> 00:03:13.710
Sheesh.

00:03:14.080 --> 00:03:15.750
Well, all right.

00:03:16.630 --> 00:03:17.800
What's wrong, Chunta?

00:03:17.800 --> 00:03:20.300
Takato, please wait here.

00:03:20.630 --> 00:03:21.470
Okay.

00:03:26.430 --> 00:03:27.260
Toy Poodle, Male,
2 Years Old
Maron

00:03:26.430 --> 00:03:30.180
Cut it out. If you eat something weird,
Reiko will be pissed at me.

00:03:27.970 --> 00:03:29.020
Japan Arts Enterprise
Chihiro Ayagi

00:03:32.390 --> 00:03:34.360
Ow! Let go of me!

00:03:34.730 --> 00:03:37.900
Damn it! Why am I walking a dog
when I've come all the way to Hawaii?

00:03:39.690 --> 00:03:43.410
<i>I'm going shopping,
so please take care of Maron, Chi.</i>

00:03:40.190 --> 00:03:42.400
Venus Inc., Owner
Reiko

00:03:43.700 --> 00:03:45.780
<i>Sure!</i>

00:03:47.080 --> 00:03:51.330
I'm here to make amends for the break-ups,
but also being a bootlicker isn't easy.

00:03:51.500 --> 00:03:54.920
<i>Still, how many more people
do I have to go through?</i>

00:03:54.920 --> 00:03:58.460
Daisuke! Mi! Where are you?!

00:04:00.300 --> 00:04:02.090
What the hell, man!

00:04:07.930 --> 00:04:10.600
- Here you go.
- What's that?

00:04:10.930 --> 00:04:13.560
I don't know. I bought it at that stall.

00:04:13.810 --> 00:04:17.690
I thought the black one would suit you more.
I got the white one, so we match!

00:04:17.900 --> 00:04:19.900
Wait, but I don't want it.

00:04:19.900 --> 00:04:21.070
It's kind of creepy.

00:04:21.240 --> 00:04:24.820
Don't be like that. Just take it!
Okay? Here.

00:04:24.820 --> 00:04:26.620
I said I don't want it!

00:04:26.910 --> 00:04:29.200
It's to commemorate our first beach date!

00:04:29.200 --> 00:04:30.660
Knock it off. Are you a moron?

00:04:31.290 --> 00:04:32.660
I'm sorry!

00:04:32.910 --> 00:04:34.290
What's that racket?

00:04:34.460 --> 00:04:36.290
I didn't mean to do it!

00:04:35.120 --> 00:04:37.420
Galaxy Agency
Ryo Narumiya

00:04:36.290 --> 00:04:39.090
Hawaiian god,
I'm sorry that I wasted food!

00:04:39.090 --> 00:04:41.300
That's what you care about, you little brat?

00:04:41.760 --> 00:04:43.590
And I'm sorry to you too, Mr. Ayagi!

00:04:43.590 --> 00:04:45.380
Why do I get second billing?

00:04:46.760 --> 00:04:49.600
Hey, was there a special sale
on coincidences today?

00:04:54.060 --> 00:04:57.020
So we're here for work.

00:04:57.020 --> 00:04:59.060
What are you two doing here?

00:04:59.320 --> 00:05:01.360
I'm here on my class trip.

00:05:01.360 --> 00:05:04.610
It's free time, but I lost sight of my friends.

00:05:04.610 --> 00:05:07.950
And then, as I was wandering around,
Mr. Ayagi crashed into my ice cream.

00:05:08.740 --> 00:05:10.080
You liar!

00:05:10.450 --> 00:05:15.210
You were panicking, lost, and crying out
for your friends, when you walked right into me!

00:05:15.210 --> 00:05:18.210
After all, I don't speak English,
and I was all alone!

00:05:18.210 --> 00:05:19.500
I was on the verge of tears!

00:05:19.500 --> 00:05:22.000
The hell do I care?
What are you gonna do about this?

00:05:22.000 --> 00:05:23.460
My shirt's all sticky!

00:05:23.760 --> 00:05:26.760
Well? How are you gonna make this right?

00:05:26.760 --> 00:05:28.720
Geez, I already apologized!

00:05:28.720 --> 00:05:33.020
Hey, don't pick on the youngster.
He'll see how small-minded you are.

00:05:33.020 --> 00:05:34.930
I don't want to hear that from you.

00:05:35.310 --> 00:05:37.020
So what are you doing here?

00:05:39.190 --> 00:05:41.650
Well, it's not so much work
as I came with someone.

00:05:41.650 --> 00:05:43.940
You could say I'm trying to clean up my act.

00:05:44.400 --> 00:05:47.780
Oh? Could it be that it's still going on?

00:05:47.780 --> 00:05:48.780
The pillow-talk—

00:05:49.030 --> 00:05:50.200
No, it's not!

00:05:50.200 --> 00:05:52.660
I told you I'm trying to clean up my act,
you malicious angel!

00:05:52.950 --> 00:05:58.080
Geez. Saijo, why not dump this dangerous guy
and switch over to me?

00:05:58.080 --> 00:06:01.290
Right now, stability and sincerity
are my selling points.

00:06:01.290 --> 00:06:02.750
- Ayagi!
- Ow!

00:06:03.090 --> 00:06:06.260
Instead of always making gross jokes at me,

00:06:06.260 --> 00:06:09.640
I told you to make 100 friends,
you poor lonely bastard!

00:06:09.640 --> 00:06:10.680
Shoo, shoo!

00:06:11.470 --> 00:06:13.930
Mr. Ayagi, you're lonely?

00:06:13.930 --> 00:06:16.100
Want me to become your friend?

00:06:20.190 --> 00:06:23.360
This is all your fault, you pretend-angel!

00:06:25.860 --> 00:06:27.490
I found a volleyball!

00:06:27.490 --> 00:06:30.030
Oh, there's a sand court over there.

00:06:30.030 --> 00:06:31.820
A court?! Seriously?!

00:06:31.820 --> 00:06:33.740
I want to play beach volleyball!

00:06:34.120 --> 00:06:36.500
Well, I don't tan, so...

00:06:37.250 --> 00:06:40.460
Sounds to me like you don't have
any confidence in your athletic skills.

00:06:40.750 --> 00:06:44.420
Says the guy who took forever
to make our sword battle look good.

00:06:45.460 --> 00:06:49.300
Fine! I'll wipe that smirk right off your face!

00:06:49.590 --> 00:06:51.550
Yep, I knew you'd take the bait.

00:06:51.890 --> 00:06:53.180
Takato, what about our date?

00:06:53.180 --> 00:06:55.680
Come on! Get ready, you guys!

00:06:55.680 --> 00:06:56.600
Yay!

00:06:56.600 --> 00:06:58.430
Takato!

00:07:03.860 --> 00:07:05.190
Dude, you're taking this too seriously!

00:07:05.190 --> 00:07:06.070
I'll kill you!

00:07:06.070 --> 00:07:06.900
You'll kill me?!

00:07:07.150 --> 00:07:08.570
Hang in there, Mr. Ayagi!

00:07:08.570 --> 00:07:11.660
Things might be tough and sad,
but all's fair on the court!

00:07:11.820 --> 00:07:13.910
You get the ball, too! We're a team, right?

00:07:13.910 --> 00:07:15.660
Are you eating ice cream again?!

00:07:15.660 --> 00:07:16.490
Here we go!

00:07:16.490 --> 00:07:17.830
- Set the ball, Chunta!
- Right!

00:07:19.460 --> 00:07:23.330
<i>Damn it, he's a pretty boy on the outside
and springs on the inside!</i>

00:07:23.330 --> 00:07:26.000
<i>My knees are trembling!</i>

00:07:27.130 --> 00:07:28.800
Give me a break already, superstar.

00:07:32.470 --> 00:07:33.470
Ow.

00:07:34.300 --> 00:07:35.800
Ow.

00:07:35.800 --> 00:07:38.220
<i>It's like I pushed him down!</i>

00:07:38.770 --> 00:07:40.140
A-Ayagi.

00:07:40.140 --> 00:07:41.350
<i>Whoa, whoa, whoa!</i>

00:07:41.350 --> 00:07:42.810
<i>What's that gap about?</i>

00:07:42.810 --> 00:07:43.770
Ayagi?

00:07:43.770 --> 00:07:46.980
<i>Why do you look so aroused, Takato?</i>

00:07:46.980 --> 00:07:47.980
<i>I'll cornhole you!</i>

00:07:48.230 --> 00:07:50.820
<i>This is an accident, right?
Yeah, just a coincidence.</i>

00:07:51.320 --> 00:07:53.950
<i>It wouldn't count if I touched him just a little.</i>

00:07:54.320 --> 00:07:56.780
<i>By the way, Chihiro Ayagi,</i>

00:07:56.780 --> 00:08:00.450
<i>I've heard rumors that you pillow-talked
your way up the ladder. Is that true?</i>

00:08:00.450 --> 00:08:02.920
Okay, okay! I figured that was coming!

00:08:02.920 --> 00:08:04.420
Give me that, geez!

00:08:05.420 --> 00:08:09.130
That bastard.
How many of these toys does he have?

00:08:09.670 --> 00:08:11.760
Takato, are you all right?

00:08:12.760 --> 00:08:13.840
I ate sand!

00:08:15.300 --> 00:08:17.010
That might be enough.

00:08:18.060 --> 00:08:20.850
What's that now?
What about "pillows" again?

00:08:20.850 --> 00:08:22.430
You're hearing things! Forget about it.

00:08:22.430 --> 00:08:24.480
Now let's get back to the game!

00:08:25.770 --> 00:08:27.060
Hey, what are you doing?

00:08:27.060 --> 00:08:28.360
Are you really trying?

00:08:28.360 --> 00:08:29.940
Sorry! I'll get it!

00:08:30.440 --> 00:08:33.070
Um, I think it went over here.

00:08:34.200 --> 00:08:35.160
Chunta!

00:08:35.160 --> 00:08:36.200
I'll check on him!

00:08:36.200 --> 00:08:37.620
Takato!

00:08:41.120 --> 00:08:43.540
Hey, Chunta, where are you?

00:08:43.540 --> 00:08:44.580
Are you okay?

00:08:45.370 --> 00:08:47.540
Takato! I'm over here!

00:08:47.540 --> 00:08:48.710
Over where?

00:08:50.300 --> 00:08:51.300
Chun...

00:08:52.380 --> 00:08:54.090
This was on purpose?

00:08:54.090 --> 00:08:55.550
Yes, I did it on purpose.

00:08:55.550 --> 00:08:59.260
Because we're supposed to be on a date,
and you're not paying me any attention.

00:08:59.260 --> 00:09:00.510
This is not a date!

00:09:00.510 --> 00:09:03.140
I want to be alone with you, Takato.

00:09:04.310 --> 00:09:05.900
We can do that when we get back!

00:09:05.900 --> 00:09:10.770
This is different. In Hawaii, we can have
a date here and not have to worry about it.

00:09:11.030 --> 00:09:14.240
I did some digging
and put together a date itinerary.

00:09:14.740 --> 00:09:15.570
What do you think?

00:09:17.620 --> 00:09:18.620
I see. I see.

00:09:19.410 --> 00:09:21.620
Well, I can't say I'm not interested...

00:09:22.660 --> 00:09:24.120
So now that it's settled, let's go!

00:09:25.290 --> 00:09:27.170
Let's make some memories, just you and me!

00:09:28.080 --> 00:09:29.210
Put me down!

00:09:29.210 --> 00:09:31.550
Let go of me! You kidnapper!

00:09:32.090 --> 00:09:33.590
Did you hear something?

00:09:33.590 --> 00:09:35.050
Mr. Ayagi! Mr. Ayagi!

00:09:35.050 --> 00:09:36.550
I want to have some ice cream!

00:09:36.720 --> 00:09:38.550
You just had some!

00:09:44.890 --> 00:09:46.640
I finally found you!

00:09:46.640 --> 00:09:50.020
I thought maybe I'd never see you guys again!

00:09:50.020 --> 00:09:52.270
It's your own fault for wandering off.

00:09:50.440 --> 00:09:52.270
Ryo Narumiya's Friend
Daisuke Ueno

00:09:52.440 --> 00:09:54.190
We looked all over for you.

00:09:54.190 --> 00:09:57.700
All right! Now that we found Naru,
let's go somewhere.

00:09:55.360 --> 00:09:57.700
Narumiya's Friend
Ryota Iriya

00:09:55.360 --> 00:09:57.700
Narumiya's Friend
Michiru Miwa

00:09:57.700 --> 00:09:58.700
Where should we go?

00:09:59.370 --> 00:10:00.450
No ideas?

00:10:01.240 --> 00:10:03.080
You should've looked into it.

00:10:03.080 --> 00:10:05.700
This is our free time, and that time is limited.

00:10:05.700 --> 00:10:07.290
Look who's talking!

00:10:07.290 --> 00:10:09.290
We have to do this next!

00:10:09.290 --> 00:10:12.090
Look, it's got a recommended rating of 90%!

00:10:17.970 --> 00:10:20.140
Hurry up, Takato!

00:10:20.390 --> 00:10:23.560
There's no rush.
The dolphins aren't going to escape.

00:10:23.560 --> 00:10:25.720
As long as we're here,
I want to get good seats!

00:10:26.100 --> 00:10:28.100
Sheesh, you're like a little kid.

00:10:35.320 --> 00:10:36.400
Did you see that?

00:10:36.400 --> 00:10:37.610
Yes, I'm watching right now.

00:10:37.990 --> 00:10:39.530
How cute!

00:10:39.660 --> 00:10:42.240
Yeah, you sure are.

00:10:42.830 --> 00:10:43.450
What?

00:10:45.660 --> 00:10:46.500
Hey!

00:10:46.500 --> 00:10:48.710
Huh?! Mr. Saijo and Junta!

00:10:50.540 --> 00:10:53.130
S-So you're here! Are those your friends?

00:10:53.460 --> 00:10:55.840
Yes! We were safely reunited!

00:10:56.130 --> 00:10:58.420
N-No way, is that Takato?

00:10:59.220 --> 00:11:00.130
Nice to meet you.

00:11:00.300 --> 00:11:02.600
And there's Junta Azumaya!

00:11:02.600 --> 00:11:04.220
"Mister," you idiot! Mr. Azumaya!

00:11:04.970 --> 00:11:07.680
Imagine meeting in a place like this.
Good to know you.

00:11:08.060 --> 00:11:09.690
He's an angel!

00:11:09.690 --> 00:11:11.150
An angel in our midst!

00:11:11.520 --> 00:11:13.900
I know! Let's take a photo!

00:11:15.820 --> 00:11:17.190
Ready? Cheese!

00:11:23.160 --> 00:11:24.660
See you!

00:11:27.450 --> 00:11:28.290
What's wrong?

00:11:28.620 --> 00:11:31.000
Nothing.
Come on. Let's go to the next place!

00:11:42.760 --> 00:11:44.390
I want to go here!

00:11:43.510 --> 00:11:46.390
<i>Sheesh. Where did Reiko go?</i>

00:11:44.390 --> 00:11:45.300
What is it?

00:11:45.300 --> 00:11:47.560
Since we're in Hawaii, we have to see it!

00:11:46.390 --> 00:11:49.810
<i>It'll be a pain if we don't meet up eventually.</i>

00:11:47.560 --> 00:11:49.810
It's a show that we can't miss!

00:12:00.530 --> 00:12:02.150
Aloha!

00:12:05.240 --> 00:12:07.200
W-Wow!

00:12:07.200 --> 00:12:08.240
It's something, huh?

00:12:08.790 --> 00:12:10.000
That's hot!

00:12:10.000 --> 00:12:11.120
Are you okay?

00:12:11.120 --> 00:12:14.330
Oh, I was just surprised.
No big deal. See?

00:12:15.210 --> 00:12:16.340
That's no good.

00:12:16.340 --> 00:12:18.380
I'd better disinfect it, just in case.

00:12:20.420 --> 00:12:21.880
He's here, too?

00:12:27.470 --> 00:12:28.760
Watch out!

00:12:33.190 --> 00:12:34.560
Hot!

00:12:35.600 --> 00:12:37.310
My hair!

00:12:39.780 --> 00:12:40.860
You...

00:12:41.820 --> 00:12:43.110
Heartwarming!

00:12:43.110 --> 00:12:44.240
Animal lover!

00:12:46.780 --> 00:12:47.620
What?

00:12:47.870 --> 00:12:48.910
Nice job!

00:12:48.910 --> 00:12:50.080
Amazing!

00:12:50.240 --> 00:12:52.040
Good job!

00:12:57.290 --> 00:13:00.250
You can't come to Hawaii and not surf! Right?

00:13:01.460 --> 00:13:02.920
Is something wrong?

00:13:03.130 --> 00:13:04.510
N-Nothing's wrong!

00:13:04.510 --> 00:13:08.140
Takato, I'm afraid to ask,
but you can swim, right?

00:13:08.140 --> 00:13:09.390
Of course I can swim!

00:13:09.720 --> 00:13:15.100
I figured as much. You're perfect, so naturally
that includes being able to swim, right?

00:13:15.100 --> 00:13:16.270
It goes without saying!

00:13:16.270 --> 00:13:18.400
I hope we get some big waves!

00:13:19.230 --> 00:13:22.860
<i>Easy to say, but will I really be okay?</i>

00:13:23.240 --> 00:13:25.820
<i>I'm sure my feet won't touch the bottom here.</i>

00:13:28.490 --> 00:13:31.240
<i>Damn it, why does
he have to be good at everything?</i>

00:13:31.450 --> 00:13:33.620
Takato, here comes a nice wave!

00:13:34.120 --> 00:13:37.580
<i>N-No way! I can’t! I can’t! I can't!</i>

00:13:38.170 --> 00:13:39.790
Yeah, now! Stand up!

00:13:40.590 --> 00:13:41.710
<i>Like I can.</i>

00:13:42.050 --> 00:13:43.630
<i>All right, whatever!</i>

00:13:45.380 --> 00:13:47.090
<i>I'm standing!
How could I doubt myself?</i>

00:13:49.680 --> 00:13:50.510
Takato!

00:14:01.980 --> 00:14:03.190
Takato!

00:14:03.570 --> 00:14:05.240
I'm saved?

00:14:05.860 --> 00:14:07.450
I thought I was going to die.

00:14:07.860 --> 00:14:10.660
It's okay. I'll always save you.

00:14:11.910 --> 00:14:13.080
Chunta.

00:14:16.790 --> 00:14:19.670
Huh?! Fancy meeting you guys again!

00:14:19.670 --> 00:14:22.960
She's gone! Where are you, Reiko?

00:14:33.970 --> 00:14:35.680
This looks delicious!

00:14:35.680 --> 00:14:37.430
Yeah, sure does.

00:14:37.430 --> 00:14:41.730
Running into you guys in this huge Hawaii
again and again, it's like fate!

00:14:41.730 --> 00:14:44.230
We should all just go sightseeing
somewhere together!

00:14:44.230 --> 00:14:46.610
Brats should play with fellow brats.

00:14:46.610 --> 00:14:49.780
Mr. Saijo, how about going drinking after this?

00:14:49.780 --> 00:14:52.070
No, I'm heading back to the hotel to relax.

00:14:52.070 --> 00:14:54.830
Takato has somewhere to go with me after this.

00:14:55.450 --> 00:14:58.040
Sorry, but do you mind if we split up?

00:14:59.420 --> 00:15:00.250
Sure.

00:15:00.460 --> 00:15:01.460
No problem!

00:15:07.720 --> 00:15:09.630
It's like you said.

00:15:09.630 --> 00:15:12.220
This is a quiet, beautiful beach, Chunta.

00:15:12.220 --> 00:15:14.260
It is, Takato.

00:15:16.180 --> 00:15:18.430
- Nobody else is here.
- True.

00:15:20.190 --> 00:15:22.270
Just you and me?

00:15:22.270 --> 00:15:23.110
Yes.

00:15:26.110 --> 00:15:26.940
So...

00:15:27.650 --> 00:15:29.400
now what are we supposed to do?

00:15:29.400 --> 00:15:30.820
We're stuck here!

00:15:30.820 --> 00:15:32.200
I-I'm sorry!

00:15:32.200 --> 00:15:34.830
I didn't know the path
disappeared during high tide!

00:15:34.990 --> 00:15:36.950
Crap. No service on my phone either.

00:15:36.950 --> 00:15:38.410
It's hopeless, huh?

00:15:38.870 --> 00:15:41.500
I really am sorry, Takato.

00:15:42.580 --> 00:15:44.290
You don't look too sorry!

00:15:44.460 --> 00:15:46.420
You look happy!

00:15:47.380 --> 00:15:51.260
When I thought that it really is just
the two of us here, I couldn't help but smile.

00:15:51.680 --> 00:15:54.470
Doesn't it feel like we're
the last two people on Earth?

00:15:56.810 --> 00:15:58.810
You're pleased by the stupidest things.

00:15:58.810 --> 00:16:02.770
If we were the last two people on Earth,
who would watch my work?

00:16:02.770 --> 00:16:03.730
Good point.

00:16:03.980 --> 00:16:07.270
We can go back once the tide is out,
so what should we do until then?

00:16:07.530 --> 00:16:09.650
Sleep on the beach tonight?

00:16:09.650 --> 00:16:12.280
Oh, leave that to me!

00:16:16.660 --> 00:16:18.790
Want me to peel another mango?

00:16:18.790 --> 00:16:21.160
Nah, I'm stuffed.

00:16:21.750 --> 00:16:23.790
Anyway, what are you?

00:16:24.630 --> 00:16:27.130
You can do all this with a single utility knife.

00:16:27.380 --> 00:16:30.800
Oh, I once had a part-time job
on a desert island.

00:16:30.800 --> 00:16:31.800
What kind of part-time job?

00:16:32.340 --> 00:16:37.890
I guess I just pick up skills like this.
I'm glad it's become helpful for you.

00:16:38.100 --> 00:16:40.680
Yeah, I'm grateful.

00:16:40.680 --> 00:16:43.600
Well, it's my fault we ended up here.

00:16:45.020 --> 00:16:47.360
The stars? Amazing.

00:16:51.610 --> 00:16:53.490
Takato, are you cold?

00:16:53.490 --> 00:16:56.570
Y-Yeah, that night wind is a little...

00:16:56.570 --> 00:16:57.950
But I'm fine.

00:16:58.330 --> 00:16:59.490
I'll go over there.

00:17:01.410 --> 00:17:02.410
There.

00:17:04.290 --> 00:17:06.000
<i>It's like...</i>

00:17:06.000 --> 00:17:08.960
Hey, I said I'm fine.

00:17:09.920 --> 00:17:11.760
I want to warm you up.

00:17:11.960 --> 00:17:15.680
Besides, I'm sure
you're used to sitting in my lap by now, right?

00:17:16.970 --> 00:17:20.470
<i>Ever since the day I said "I really like you,"</i>

00:17:20.470 --> 00:17:22.930
<i>whenever we act like lovers like this...</i>

00:17:22.930 --> 00:17:24.390
Don't get carried away.

00:17:24.390 --> 00:17:25.850
Just stay put.

00:17:26.810 --> 00:17:29.570
<i>I feel even more self-conscious than before.</i>

00:17:29.980 --> 00:17:32.190
<i>It's more than just getting carried away,</i>

00:17:32.190 --> 00:17:34.030
<i>and that troubles me.</i>

00:17:34.360 --> 00:17:37.450
Oh, that's right. I found an unusual flower.

00:17:37.450 --> 00:17:38.490
Look at this.

00:17:39.410 --> 00:17:43.910
This one was blooming on a hill,
and this one was blooming on the beach.

00:17:44.160 --> 00:17:49.080
They're pretty different,
but both only have petals on their bottom half.

00:17:50.420 --> 00:17:52.460
This is called "naupaka".

00:17:52.460 --> 00:17:53.300
"Naupaka"?

00:17:53.920 --> 00:17:56.130
The site coordinator told me about it.

00:17:56.470 --> 00:17:58.590
The legend of the naupaka.

00:17:59.090 --> 00:18:03.680
It seems the god of fire had fallen in love
with a man who already had a sweetheart.

00:18:03.680 --> 00:18:07.230
Fearing the god's wrath,
the man escaped to the sea

00:18:07.230 --> 00:18:11.150
while the woman escaped to the mountain,
but they were forever after separated.

00:18:11.150 --> 00:18:15.240
The naupaka blooms
in the two areas where they escaped,

00:18:15.240 --> 00:18:17.570
serving as a symbol of the tragic lovers.

00:18:18.320 --> 00:18:21.410
I wonder why they didn't go together.

00:18:22.030 --> 00:18:26.370
If they had escaped together,
they wouldn't be ripped apart like this.

00:18:28.210 --> 00:18:30.580
If it had been me, I definitely would've...

00:18:30.750 --> 00:18:32.170
- Hey!
- Ow!

00:18:32.170 --> 00:18:34.800
There's no need to take a fairy tale so seriously.

00:18:35.050 --> 00:18:38.010
You're right. What am I feeling gloomy about?

00:18:38.130 --> 00:18:39.510
Hey!

00:18:39.510 --> 00:18:45.350
Right now you're in my arms.
That's all I need to be happy.

00:18:46.100 --> 00:18:47.180
You're crushing me!

00:18:51.560 --> 00:18:53.610
We finally kissed.

00:18:55.990 --> 00:18:58.280
Takato, your neck is sunburned.

00:18:58.740 --> 00:19:00.870
Look, below your knees, too.

00:19:00.870 --> 00:19:03.160
Y-You don't have to check every spot!

00:19:03.160 --> 00:19:04.120
Don't touch me, you idiot!

00:19:04.410 --> 00:19:07.750
It's easy to see on you
because your skin is so pale.

00:19:07.750 --> 00:19:09.370
Maybe here, too?

00:19:09.370 --> 00:19:12.630
S-Stop it! You insatiable angel!

00:19:12.630 --> 00:19:14.880
I know where you're going with this!

00:19:14.880 --> 00:19:16.460
You're onto me?

00:19:16.460 --> 00:19:19.050
But we don't get many chances
where we don't have to hold back.

00:19:19.220 --> 00:19:20.380
What are you talking about?

00:19:20.380 --> 00:19:23.390
- Huh? Outdoor—
- Outdoor?! You pervert!

00:19:23.390 --> 00:19:26.560
I don't want to do it outside,
and I'm not stripping here!

00:19:26.970 --> 00:19:29.100
Oh, I see.

00:19:29.100 --> 00:19:32.690
Then I just have to put you in the mood
with our clothes on, huh?

00:19:32.690 --> 00:19:33.520
Roger that.

00:19:36.480 --> 00:19:38.240
W-W-W-We're outside!

00:19:38.240 --> 00:19:40.950
It's okay.
I won't take off your clothes. I promise.

00:19:41.070 --> 00:19:43.820
P-Promise? None of this is okay!

00:19:44.620 --> 00:19:45.990
Then I should take off your clothes?

00:19:45.990 --> 00:19:48.540
No, you... H-Hey, hands off.

00:19:48.540 --> 00:19:50.040
Hands off my swim trunks!

00:19:50.920 --> 00:19:54.130
<i>Stop it. This is embarrassing.
Any more and you'll make me...</i>

00:19:54.790 --> 00:19:59.630
Takato, recently you haven't been
showing me your face so much.

00:19:59.630 --> 00:20:02.050
And you hold your voice back. What's wrong?

00:20:02.050 --> 00:20:03.840
<i>Shut up! Don't get so close to me!</i>

00:20:04.550 --> 00:20:07.680
Please let me see you
when I'm giving you pleasure.

00:20:08.350 --> 00:20:09.850
N-No.

00:20:10.520 --> 00:20:15.190
<i>I don't know what kind of voice, or what kind
of face I should have when we're making love.</i>

00:20:15.190 --> 00:20:16.190
<i>Damn it!</i>

00:20:24.240 --> 00:20:25.910
Thank you, Chi.

00:20:25.910 --> 00:20:27.160
You were a big help.

00:20:27.160 --> 00:20:29.410
Did you two get along?

00:20:29.410 --> 00:20:31.960
Sure, we became great pals, right?

00:20:35.670 --> 00:20:37.670
Ouch! What the hell?

00:20:37.670 --> 00:20:40.010
After I saved your life!

00:20:41.800 --> 00:20:43.260
You still have a ways to go.

00:20:54.650 --> 00:20:57.610
T-Takato, are you still mad?

00:20:57.730 --> 00:21:01.240
About what? That the whole
desert island adventure was your plan,

00:21:01.240 --> 00:21:05.870
and when I got back to the hotel, I found out
you'd even informed Mr. Sasaki about it already?

00:21:05.870 --> 00:21:07.990
I just wanted to enjoy outdoor se...

00:21:07.990 --> 00:21:10.240
I mean enjoy our vacation together!

00:21:10.240 --> 00:21:13.040
Damn it, you set me up every time.

00:21:13.040 --> 00:21:15.460
You're no angel, you're a trickster crow!

00:21:18.590 --> 00:21:21.840
Takato, that was a good one! Amazing!

00:21:22.300 --> 00:21:23.510
Whatever!

00:21:23.510 --> 00:21:24.840
Wait for me!

00:21:27.760 --> 00:21:29.350
Two men, huh?

00:21:27.760 --> 00:21:29.680
Independent Cameraman
Jiro Hasegawa

00:21:29.350 --> 00:21:31.270
That makes a boring picture.

00:21:31.430 --> 00:21:36.480
All right,
time to get serious about making money.

00:21:36.900 --> 00:21:39.440
Good work today. How'd it go over there?

00:21:37.400 --> 00:21:39.440
TV-J Director
Daisuke Oki

00:21:39.980 --> 00:21:42.820
Yeah, we kept up our acquaintance.

00:21:40.650 --> 00:21:42.820
TV-J General Producer
Kazuomi Usaka

00:21:43.360 --> 00:21:44.400
What's wrong?

00:21:45.280 --> 00:21:46.110
Nothing.

00:21:51.830 --> 00:21:53.160
It's nothing.

00:21:53.540 --> 00:21:54.710
Shall we go?

00:23:25.750 --> 00:23:27.420
Chunta.

00:23:27.590 --> 00:23:28.630
Takato.

00:23:28.630 --> 00:23:31.590
I don't believe it.

00:23:31.590 --> 00:23:33.680
No, that was a dream.

00:23:33.680 --> 00:23:36.970
It must've been a dream.
But don't tell me he...

00:23:37.220 --> 00:23:40.020
hug9
"...I guess you two are close."
